WEBVTT

00:00:06.313 --> 00:00:12.755
One day, a postman came to my village.

00:00:12.815 --> 00:00:27.848
The postman brought me a letter from my son, Song.

00:00:27.908 --> 00:00:37.058
Is your name, Adam?"

00:00:37.118 --> 00:00:38.709
The postman asked.

00:00:38.769 --> 00:00:40.669
Yes, I said.

00:00:40.729 --> 00:00:42.940
I've got a letter for you.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:45.671
The postman read the envelope.

00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:48.912
Adam of the village of Minta.

00:00:48.972 --> 00:00:51.032
A letter for me?

00:00:51.092 --> 00:00:52.682
Who is it from?

00:00:52.742 --> 00:00:54.193
I asked.

00:00:54.253 --> 00:00:57.604
The postman looked at the envelope again.

00:00:57.664 --> 00:01:00.754
From Saul, he said.

00:01:00.814 --> 00:01:05.471
He gave me the letter and walked away.

00:01:05.531 --> 00:01:08.627
Martha!

00:01:08.687 --> 00:01:09.657
Martha!

00:01:09.677 --> 00:01:11.748
I called to my wife.

00:01:11.808 --> 00:01:12.908
Come here!

00:01:12.968 --> 00:01:16.809
We have a letter from our son's soul!

00:01:16.869 --> 00:01:20.430
Martha came out and looked at the letter.

00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:24.461
She was excited, but she was also worried.

00:01:24.521 --> 00:01:27.882
A letter from soul, she said.

00:01:27.941 --> 00:01:30.152
Is he alive and well?

00:01:30.212 --> 00:01:32.833
I'm going to find the schoolteacher.

00:01:32.893 --> 00:01:35.276
He can read the letter.

00:01:35.336 --> 00:01:42.142
There was no school 50 years ago, so I cannot read or write.

00:01:42.202 --> 00:01:44.574
I live in a small village.

00:01:44.634 --> 00:01:47.056
The only work is farming.

00:01:47.116 --> 00:01:54.271
My only son, Saul, left the village two years ago, and my three daughters are married.

00:01:54.331 --> 00:01:59.064
Saul is making a lot of money in a foreign country.

00:01:59.124 --> 00:02:03.126
Martha and the school teacher came back.

00:02:03.186 --> 00:02:05.395
A lot of other people came.

00:02:05.455 --> 00:02:08.745
Everyone wanted to hear my letter.

00:02:08.804 --> 00:02:17.051
The school teacher opened the envelope and read the letter.

00:02:17.111 --> 00:02:28.000
Twenty Taylor Street, London E19, England 16th of March.

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:32.073
Dear father, I am living in London.

00:02:32.133 --> 00:02:34.854
I have a job in a factory.

00:02:34.914 --> 00:02:37.135
The work is very hard.

00:02:37.195 --> 00:02:42.028
I often work at night, but the pay is good.

00:02:42.088 --> 00:02:46.670
I am well, and I live with people from my country.

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:51.892
I am sending you 100 pounds in this letter.

00:02:51.952 --> 00:02:55.234
This is for you and my mother.

00:02:55.294 --> 00:02:59.036
Love to you and mother, soul.

00:02:59.056 --> 00:03:03.585
100 pounds.

00:03:03.645 --> 00:03:07.613
I said to the school teacher, you're wrong.

00:03:07.673 --> 00:03:09.343
It's a mistake.

00:03:09.403 --> 00:03:13.484
No, the school teacher said, I'm not wrong.

00:03:13.544 --> 00:03:15.064
It's not a mistake.

00:03:15.124 --> 00:03:16.865
Here is the money.

00:03:16.925 --> 00:03:19.835
And he gave me a piece of paper.

00:03:19.895 --> 00:03:21.476
What is this?

00:03:21.536 --> 00:03:24.546
I asked a money order.

00:03:24.606 --> 00:03:28.137
The school teacher said, go to Darpur.

00:03:28.197 --> 00:03:32.719
Take this money order to the post office in Darpur.

00:03:32.779 --> 00:03:36.852
The money order is worth 100 pounds.

00:03:36.912 --> 00:03:41.826
The post office official will give you the money.

00:03:41.846 --> 00:03:45.338
100 pounds, I said again.

00:03:45.398 --> 00:03:50.512
Everyone laughed and said, Adam, you are a rich man.

00:03:50.572 --> 00:03:54.504
You can buy many things for your farm and for your house.

00:03:54.564 --> 00:03:59.388
And I can buy some good food and drink in Tarpur.

00:03:59.448 --> 00:04:02.677
I am going to give a party for you all.

00:04:02.737 --> 00:04:04.806
I told my friends.

00:04:04.866 --> 00:04:11.974
Martha said, soul is a good son.

00:04:12.033 --> 00:04:20.092
That evening, the village people talked about the money order and my money.

00:04:20.152 --> 00:04:23.455
Martha and I also talked about the money.

00:04:23.515 --> 00:04:33.545
We needed many things for the farm.

00:04:33.605 --> 00:04:46.563
Chapter 2, Adam goes to Darpur.

00:04:46.623 --> 00:04:51.244
The next morning I got up very early.

00:04:51.304 --> 00:04:57.195
It was dark, and everyone was asleep, but I was going to Darpur.

00:04:57.255 --> 00:05:00.195
I washed and dressed carefully.

00:05:00.255 --> 00:05:05.196
I put on my best clothes, and I carried my best stick.

00:05:05.216 --> 00:05:11.044
I put the money order carefully in my pocket, and I said goodbye to Martha.

00:05:11.104 --> 00:05:15.094
I walked ten miles to the main road.

00:05:15.154 --> 00:05:20.488
I sat down at the main road and ate my breakfast.

00:05:20.548 --> 00:05:24.000
I waited for the bus.

00:05:24.060 --> 00:05:27.073
I waited for two hours.

00:05:27.132 --> 00:05:33.908
Then the bus came and I got on.

00:05:33.968 --> 00:05:40.042
It is a long way to Darpour.

00:05:40.102 --> 00:05:43.084
The bus takes three hours.

00:05:43.143 --> 00:05:48.136
I arrived in Darpur and walked to the post office immediately.

00:05:48.196 --> 00:05:50.887
I do not often go to Darpur.

00:05:50.947 --> 00:05:54.078
I only know the market and one shop.

00:05:54.138 --> 00:05:56.250
This is the shop of Rick.

00:05:56.309 --> 00:05:59.631
I buy things for my farm from Rick.

00:05:59.691 --> 00:06:03.102
There were a lot of people in the post office.

00:06:03.162 --> 00:06:05.964
I asked about money orders.

00:06:06.024 --> 00:06:08.536
A man showed me the queue.

00:06:08.596 --> 00:06:14.300
There was a long line of people, and I waited at the back.

00:06:14.360 --> 00:06:17.891
Finally, it was my turn.

00:06:17.951 --> 00:06:20.212
I was at the front of the queue.

00:06:20.272 --> 00:06:23.424
But the officials did not serve me.

00:06:23.484 --> 00:06:26.975
Excuse me, I said, it's my turn.

00:06:27.035 --> 00:06:28.346
I'm next.

00:06:28.406 --> 00:06:30.167
You're next?

00:06:30.227 --> 00:06:32.717
Oh man, I'm very busy.

00:06:32.777 --> 00:06:35.298
The official said, look at my papers.

00:06:35.358 --> 00:06:37.130
Look at all these people.

00:06:37.190 --> 00:06:41.393
I am very busy and you must wait."

00:06:41.453 --> 00:06:43.965
So I waited.

00:06:44.025 --> 00:06:47.188
Finally the official looked at me.

00:06:47.248 --> 00:06:48.729
What do you want?

00:06:48.789 --> 00:06:49.990
He asked.

00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:52.232
I gave him my money order.

00:06:52.292 --> 00:06:57.086
This is my money order for one hundred pounds, I replied.

00:06:57.145 --> 00:06:59.728
The official held out his hand.

00:06:59.788 --> 00:07:01.510
Identity card?

00:07:01.570 --> 00:07:03.177
He said.

00:07:03.236 --> 00:07:04.894
Excuse me?

00:07:04.914 --> 00:07:08.248
I don't understand, I replied.

00:07:08.308 --> 00:07:14.784
Your identity card, the official said again, give me your identity card.

00:07:14.844 --> 00:07:17.626
What is an identity card?

00:07:17.686 --> 00:07:18.916
I asked.

00:07:18.975 --> 00:07:22.836
I can't give you any money for this money order.

00:07:22.896 --> 00:07:25.889
First I must see your identity card.

00:07:25.949 --> 00:07:29.591
Your identity card gives your name and your address.

00:07:29.651 --> 00:07:32.414
Your identity card describes you.

00:07:32.474 --> 00:07:35.616
There is a photograph of you in your identity card.

00:07:35.676 --> 00:07:37.127
I don't know you.

00:07:37.187 --> 00:07:38.708
Who are you?

00:07:38.768 --> 00:07:41.440
The official was a little angry.

00:07:41.500 --> 00:07:43.692
But I was also angry.

00:07:43.751 --> 00:07:45.052
Who am I?

00:07:45.112 --> 00:07:47.584
I said, everyone knows me.

00:07:47.643 --> 00:07:50.305
I am Adam of the village of Minter.

00:07:50.365 --> 00:07:55.348
I haven't got an identity card and I don't need an identity card.

00:07:55.408 --> 00:07:59.872
Oh man, I'm very busy and you're very stupid.

00:07:59.932 --> 00:08:02.354
The official said, who are you?

00:08:02.414 --> 00:08:04.026
Where is Minter?

00:08:04.085 --> 00:08:05.647
Give me my money.

00:08:05.707 --> 00:08:07.838
Give me my £100.

00:08:07.898 --> 00:08:09.660
I said.

00:08:09.720 --> 00:08:15.845
The official looked angry and said, show me your identity card.

00:08:15.905 --> 00:08:18.136
I don't know you.

00:08:18.196 --> 00:08:24.000
The official gave back my money order, and he turned away.

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:27.524
Where can I buy an identity card?

00:08:27.583 --> 00:08:29.276
I asked the official.

00:08:29.335 --> 00:08:31.218
He did not speak to me.

00:08:31.278 --> 00:08:33.160
He did not answer.

00:08:33.220 --> 00:08:37.324
Go to the Ministry of the Interior, a man said.

00:08:37.384 --> 00:08:48.856
He was standing in the queue, and he told me the way.

00:08:48.916 --> 00:09:01.046
Chapter 3 An Identity Card.

00:09:01.106 --> 00:09:05.240
I walked to the Ministry of the Interior.

00:09:05.300 --> 00:09:07.812
I waited in another queue.

00:09:07.872 --> 00:09:10.634
I spoke to another official.

00:09:10.694 --> 00:09:13.646
I asked for an identity card.

00:09:13.706 --> 00:09:21.962
Fill in this application form, the official said, and bring the form and three photographs of yourself and two pounds.

00:09:22.022 --> 00:09:23.814
Come back tomorrow.

00:09:23.874 --> 00:09:26.126
Tomorrow, I said.

00:09:26.186 --> 00:09:29.039
Can I have an identity card today, please?

00:09:29.099 --> 00:09:30.149
I live in Minter.

00:09:30.209 --> 00:09:32.811
I live five hours' journey from Darpur.

00:09:32.871 --> 00:09:34.432
I'm an old man.

00:09:34.492 --> 00:09:36.854
Yes, come back tomorrow.

00:09:36.914 --> 00:09:40.256
And the official turned away.

00:09:40.316 --> 00:09:45.079
I walked away from the Ministry of the Interior.

00:09:45.139 --> 00:09:47.130
I walked to the market.

00:09:47.190 --> 00:09:49.822
At the market, I looked at everyone.

00:09:49.882 --> 00:09:52.534
I was looking for a man from my village.

00:09:52.594 --> 00:09:54.901
But I could not find a villager.

00:09:54.961 --> 00:09:58.028
So then I walked to the shop of Rick.

00:09:58.088 --> 00:09:59.929
I spoke to Rick.

00:09:59.989 --> 00:10:03.270
I want an identity card, I told him.

00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:06.512
But I need three photographs of myself.

00:10:06.572 --> 00:10:10.233
I see you need some photographs.

00:10:10.294 --> 00:10:15.526
And he showed me the way to a photographer.

00:10:15.586 --> 00:10:19.268
I found the house.

00:10:19.328 --> 00:10:23.132
The photographer was asleep, but he came to me quickly.

00:10:23.192 --> 00:10:27.277
The man's clothes were dirty and he looked tired.

00:10:27.338 --> 00:10:30.459
I need an identity card," I said.

00:10:30.519 --> 00:10:33.480
I want three photographs of myself.

00:10:33.541 --> 00:10:41.494
Yes, you want three photographs of yourself, the photographer replied, and I take very good photographs.

00:10:41.554 --> 00:10:43.646
Come and see my camera.

00:10:43.706 --> 00:10:46.076
We walked into his room.

00:10:46.137 --> 00:10:49.008
In the middle of the room was a large camera.

00:10:49.068 --> 00:10:52.046
This is the best camera in Darpur.

00:10:52.106 --> 00:10:55.354
This camera is very, very good.

00:10:55.414 --> 00:10:58.244
The photographer said proudly.

00:10:58.304 --> 00:11:01.315
I've never seen a camera, I said.

00:11:01.375 --> 00:11:03.255
I don't know about cameras.

00:11:03.315 --> 00:11:06.506
Hurry up and take a photograph of me.

00:11:06.566 --> 00:11:10.737
Please do not hurry me old man.

00:11:10.797 --> 00:11:14.118
The photographer said I am an artist.

00:11:14.178 --> 00:11:17.482
And he gave me a mirror and a comb.

00:11:17.542 --> 00:11:19.206
I don't want a mirror.

00:11:19.266 --> 00:11:20.597
I don't want a comb.

00:11:20.657 --> 00:11:22.970
Please take my photograph.

00:11:23.030 --> 00:11:25.472
I'm going to minter this afternoon.

00:11:25.532 --> 00:11:27.784
And I'm in a hurry," I said.

00:11:27.844 --> 00:11:29.665
Yes, he said.

00:11:29.725 --> 00:11:31.596
But first, the price.

00:11:31.656 --> 00:11:34.880
This is the best camera in dark poor.

00:11:34.940 --> 00:11:37.082
And I'm the best photographer.

00:11:37.142 --> 00:11:41.244
Three photographs will cost you two pounds fifty.

00:11:41.304 --> 00:11:43.747
Two pounds fifty?

00:11:43.807 --> 00:11:45.565
And I laughed.

00:11:45.625 --> 00:12:43.025
two pounds fifty and pay me now please the photographer answered I did not know the price of photographs what could I do then the photographer said you're an old man for you the price is two pounds so I gave him the money and he took the photographs come back tomorrow morning he said I want my three photographs now immediately I said don't be stupid the photographer said photographs take 24 hours come back tomorrow what could I do so I said yes tomorrow morning good said the photographer now go I have a lot of work I'm very busy I went back to the bus station I sat on the bus for three hours.

00:12:43.085 --> 00:12:46.658
I walked ten miles back to my village.

00:12:46.718 --> 00:12:50.411
It was nighttime, and I was very tired.

00:12:50.472 --> 00:12:54.004
Martha and my friends were waiting for me.

00:12:54.064 --> 00:12:55.976
Where is the money?

00:12:56.036 --> 00:12:58.888
Martha asked.

00:12:58.948 --> 00:13:01.920
I have no money.

00:13:01.980 --> 00:13:04.363
I cannot change the money order.

00:13:04.422 --> 00:13:07.556
First, I must have an identity card.

00:13:07.616 --> 00:13:11.052
And I told Martha everything.

00:13:11.112 --> 00:13:16.138
Tomorrow, I'm going to dark poor again, I said.

00:13:16.198 --> 00:13:18.958
Then I did not talk again.

00:13:19.018 --> 00:13:22.839
I was very tired, and it was late at night.

00:13:22.899 --> 00:13:31.951
I lay on my bed, and I slept.

00:13:32.011 --> 00:13:38.533
Chapter four.

00:13:38.593 --> 00:13:41.480
No photographs.

00:13:41.540 --> 00:13:44.987
I woke up late the next morning.

00:13:45.047 --> 00:13:47.397
The sun was already high.

00:13:47.457 --> 00:13:50.748
I did not walk to the main road and catch a bus.

00:13:50.808 --> 00:13:54.430
All the buses go to Darpur early in the morning.

00:13:54.490 --> 00:13:57.020
So I stayed at home on Wednesday.

00:13:57.080 --> 00:13:59.241
I was still very tired.

00:13:59.301 --> 00:14:03.162
I rested and talked to the villagers about the money order.

00:14:03.222 --> 00:14:06.763
I told them about the identity card and the photographer.

00:14:06.823 --> 00:14:10.973
The school teacher said, yes, the official is correct.

00:14:11.033 --> 00:14:15.183
In a post office, you always show your identity card.

00:14:15.243 --> 00:14:21.655
The school teacher filled in my application form for an identity card.

00:14:21.715 --> 00:14:26.546
Application form for identity card.

00:14:26.606 --> 00:14:30.368
Name Adam Jami.

00:14:30.428 --> 00:14:33.938
Address, Village of Minter.

00:14:33.998 --> 00:14:37.640
Age, 72 years.

00:14:37.700 --> 00:14:49.924
Place of birth, village of minta, occupation, farmer, color of eyes, brown.

00:14:49.984 --> 00:14:54.678
On Thursday, I traveled to Darpur again.

00:14:54.738 --> 00:14:58.520
I walked to the main road and I caught a bus.

00:14:58.580 --> 00:15:03.234
In Darpur, I walked to the house of the photographer.

00:15:03.294 --> 00:15:06.286
I knocked on the door of the house.

00:15:06.346 --> 00:15:08.689
No one came to the door.

00:15:08.749 --> 00:15:11.562
I knocked again loudly with my stick.

00:15:11.622 --> 00:15:13.754
A woman opened the door.

00:15:13.814 --> 00:15:14.955
Who are you?

00:15:15.015 --> 00:15:16.026
What do you want?

00:15:16.086 --> 00:15:16.976
She asked.

00:15:17.036 --> 00:15:19.388
Can I have my photographs, please?

00:15:19.449 --> 00:15:20.189
I said.

00:15:20.249 --> 00:15:21.250
Your photographs?

00:15:21.310 --> 00:15:22.651
I have no photographs?

00:15:22.711 --> 00:15:24.182
The woman replied.

00:15:24.242 --> 00:15:26.164
I came here on Tuesday.

00:15:26.224 --> 00:15:27.866
Where is the photographer?

00:15:27.926 --> 00:15:28.866
I asked.

00:15:28.926 --> 00:15:29.747
He's out.

00:15:29.807 --> 00:15:31.148
He's not here.

00:15:31.208 --> 00:15:34.661
And the woman closed the door.

00:15:34.721 --> 00:15:37.450
I shouted at her.

00:15:37.510 --> 00:15:40.268
I'm waiting here for him.

00:15:40.328 --> 00:15:44.089
After a long time, the photographer came back.

00:15:44.149 --> 00:15:47.770
He looked tired, and he smelt a beer.

00:15:47.830 --> 00:15:50.431
Give me my photographs, I said.

00:15:50.491 --> 00:15:52.821
I have waited a long time for you.

00:15:52.881 --> 00:15:58.462
The photographer looked at me and said, I don't know you old man.

00:15:58.522 --> 00:16:01.126
What photographs are you talking about?

00:16:01.186 --> 00:16:04.682
My three photographs from my identity card.

00:16:04.742 --> 00:16:07.504
I paid you two pounds for them on Tuesday.

00:16:07.564 --> 00:16:10.826
Give me my photographs immediately or my money.

00:16:10.886 --> 00:16:13.699
Your photographs, your money.

00:16:13.759 --> 00:16:15.580
What are you talking about?

00:16:15.640 --> 00:16:16.721
The photographer said.

00:16:16.781 --> 00:16:17.812
Show me the paper.

00:16:17.872 --> 00:16:21.584
Show me the receipt for your money.

00:16:21.644 --> 00:16:24.646
My receipt?

00:16:24.706 --> 00:16:25.657
I asked.

00:16:25.717 --> 00:16:28.079
Yes, where is your receipt?

00:16:28.139 --> 00:16:29.822
The photographer asked.

00:16:29.882 --> 00:16:33.406
You didn't give me a receipt, I shouted.

00:16:33.466 --> 00:16:37.078
Give me my photographs, all my money immediately.

00:16:37.138 --> 00:16:40.519
And I hit the photographer hard with my stick.

00:16:40.579 --> 00:16:43.610
I am old, but I am still strong.

00:16:43.670 --> 00:16:46.072
The photographer fell on the ground.

00:16:46.132 --> 00:16:48.342
He shouted, help, help.

00:16:48.402 --> 00:16:50.593
This old man is killing me.

00:16:50.653 --> 00:16:53.184
And I hit him hard again.

00:16:53.244 --> 00:16:56.206
Lots of people ran out of their houses.

00:16:56.266 --> 00:17:00.036
I hit the photographer again, and two men held me.

00:17:00.096 --> 00:17:02.536
I could not get away from the two men.

00:17:02.596 --> 00:17:06.230
The photographer was very angry, and I was very angry.

00:17:06.290 --> 00:17:08.532
Lots of people were shouting.

00:17:08.592 --> 00:17:10.814
Then a policeman came.

00:17:10.874 --> 00:17:13.476
The photographer shouted to the policeman.

00:17:13.536 --> 00:17:16.529
This old man hit me three times with his stick.

00:17:16.589 --> 00:17:18.310
He's a thief and a murderer.

00:17:18.370 --> 00:17:20.012
He wants my money.

00:17:20.072 --> 00:17:25.867
The policeman held my arm and said, come with me to the police station.

00:17:25.927 --> 00:17:28.374
I did not say anything.

00:17:28.434 --> 00:17:32.190
We walked to the police station.

00:17:32.250 --> 00:17:39.713
At the police station, the policeman asked me, did you hit that man three times?

00:17:39.773 --> 00:17:41.744
Yes, I said.

00:17:41.804 --> 00:17:44.255
He didn't give me my photographs.

00:17:44.315 --> 00:17:48.356
Show me your identity card, said the policeman.

00:17:48.416 --> 00:17:50.958
I am Adam of Minter Village.

00:17:51.018 --> 00:17:55.529
I replied, and I haven't got an identity card.

00:17:55.590 --> 00:17:57.966
Old man.

00:17:58.027 --> 00:17:59.454
said the policeman.

00:17:59.514 --> 00:18:01.684
Go back to your village.

00:18:01.744 --> 00:18:03.876
Don't come here and fight.

00:18:03.936 --> 00:18:06.167
Keep out of Darpur.

00:18:06.227 --> 00:18:10.699
And he pushed me into the street.

00:18:10.759 --> 00:18:14.911
I went back to my village.

00:18:14.971 --> 00:18:20.234
I was tired and angry.

00:18:20.294 --> 00:18:24.386
Chapter five.

00:18:24.446 --> 00:18:28.024
Adam changes his money order.

00:18:28.084 --> 00:18:32.832
Next day I told my story to all the villagers.

00:18:32.892 --> 00:18:35.192
The villagers were angry.

00:18:35.252 --> 00:18:37.723
Martha was very unhappy.

00:18:37.784 --> 00:18:41.055
She said, Saul is working very hard.

00:18:41.115 --> 00:18:43.796
He is sending money and we can't have the money.

00:18:43.856 --> 00:18:45.047
What are we going to do?

00:18:45.067 --> 00:18:47.898
I did not know.

00:18:47.958 --> 00:18:52.070
Then in the evening the school teacher came to my house again.

00:18:52.130 --> 00:18:55.061
Adam, perhaps I can help you.

00:18:55.121 --> 00:18:59.249
The school teacher said, here is a letter to Mr. Schith.

00:18:59.309 --> 00:19:02.646
Mr. Chef, I said, who is he?

00:19:02.706 --> 00:19:09.259
He's an important man in Darpur, and he's a friend of my wife's cousin," replied the school teacher.

00:19:09.319 --> 00:19:11.860
This letter is to Mr. Chef.

00:19:11.920 --> 00:19:14.410
The letter is about your money order.

00:19:14.470 --> 00:19:16.772
Perhaps he can help you.

00:19:16.832 --> 00:19:22.224
I took the letter and thanked the school teacher.

00:19:22.284 --> 00:19:29.035
So I traveled to Darpur again on Saturday for the third time.

00:19:29.095 --> 00:19:33.206
After a long time, I found Mr. Sheth's house.

00:19:33.266 --> 00:19:36.428
The door was opened by a tall man.

00:19:36.488 --> 00:19:38.769
Can I see Mr. Sheth?

00:19:38.828 --> 00:19:39.959
I asked.

00:19:40.019 --> 00:19:41.330
And who are you?

00:19:41.390 --> 00:19:42.820
The tall man asked.

00:19:42.880 --> 00:19:46.262
I have a letter for Mr. Sheth, I replied.

00:19:46.322 --> 00:19:47.432
I see.

00:19:47.492 --> 00:19:49.394
Can I have the letter, please?

00:19:49.454 --> 00:19:52.004
And the tall man held out his hand.

00:19:52.064 --> 00:19:54.836
The letter is here, I said.

00:19:54.896 --> 00:19:57.157
And I took the letter out of my pocket.

00:19:57.217 --> 00:19:59.506
But I must see Mr. Sheth.

00:19:59.566 --> 00:20:04.096
Many people want to see Mr. Sheth, the tall man told me.

00:20:04.156 --> 00:20:07.848
He is a very busy man and a very important man.

00:20:07.908 --> 00:20:14.412
Mr. Sheth is not here at the moment, but give me your letter, and Mr. Sheth will read it later."

00:20:14.472 --> 00:20:17.764
I gave the tall man the letter.

00:20:17.824 --> 00:20:19.926
Then I waited.

00:20:19.986 --> 00:20:26.493
Later a large black car came, and the man went into the house.

00:20:26.554 --> 00:20:31.069
A long time later, the tall man opened the door again.

00:20:31.089 --> 00:20:36.020
"'Come in now, please, and follow me,' he said.

00:20:36.080 --> 00:20:38.822
I followed the tall man.

00:20:38.882 --> 00:20:44.244
We went into a large room with fine carpets and big chairs.

00:20:44.304 --> 00:20:46.696
Another man was in the room.

00:20:46.756 --> 00:20:47.916
He was drinking.

00:20:47.936 --> 00:20:52.298
"'This is Mr. Chef,' he said the tall man.

00:20:52.318 --> 00:20:58.422
"'I am Adam of Minter Village,' I replied.

00:20:58.482 --> 00:21:03.246
Yes, I know," said Mr. Sheth.

00:21:03.307 --> 00:21:05.007
Thank you for the letter.

00:21:05.027 --> 00:21:07.638
I hope I can help you.

00:21:07.698 --> 00:21:09.930
I like to help people.

00:21:09.990 --> 00:21:12.962
Please sit down.

00:21:13.022 --> 00:21:15.402
Mr. Sheth smiled.

00:21:15.462 --> 00:21:18.874
His clothes were new and smart.

00:21:18.934 --> 00:21:21.486
Thank you, I said.

00:21:21.546 --> 00:21:24.496
Can I see the money order, please?

00:21:24.556 --> 00:21:26.518
Mr. Sheth asked.

00:21:26.578 --> 00:21:29.896
I took the money order out of my pocket.

00:21:29.956 --> 00:21:35.146
By now the money order was dirty and looked very old.

00:21:35.206 --> 00:21:37.936
I gave it to Mr. Sheith.

00:21:37.996 --> 00:21:42.769
This money order is for one hundred pounds, I said.

00:21:42.829 --> 00:21:46.280
My son sent it from a foreign country.

00:21:46.340 --> 00:21:51.094
Mr. Sheith unfolded the money order and looked at it.

00:21:51.154 --> 00:21:55.686
You can't change this money order, he said.

00:21:55.746 --> 00:21:59.194
This money order is not worth one hundred pounds.

00:21:59.254 --> 00:22:02.592
But this money order is worth nothing.

00:22:02.653 --> 00:22:04.883
Worth nothing.

00:22:04.943 --> 00:22:08.014
Worthless, I asked.

00:22:08.074 --> 00:22:11.534
Then Mr. Sheth looked at the money order again.

00:22:11.594 --> 00:22:14.175
Yes, worthless.

00:22:14.235 --> 00:22:18.245
Your son does not understand about money orders.

00:22:18.305 --> 00:22:24.016
This money order is not correct for our country, Mr. Sheth said.

00:22:24.076 --> 00:22:31.529
Then he looked at the money order again and said, And this money order is also old.

00:22:31.590 --> 00:22:34.292
It is out of date."

00:22:34.352 --> 00:22:36.814
I said nothing.

00:22:36.875 --> 00:22:40.698
Mr. Sheth gave me the money order back.

00:22:40.758 --> 00:22:46.673
Then Mr. Sheth smiled and said, I am very sorry.

00:22:46.732 --> 00:22:48.604
You are an old man.

00:22:48.664 --> 00:22:51.356
You came a long way from your village.

00:22:51.416 --> 00:22:55.668
What can I give you to eat and drink?

00:22:55.728 --> 00:22:58.768
I was not hungry.

00:22:58.828 --> 00:23:01.580
But Mr. Sheth went out of the room.

00:23:01.640 --> 00:23:05.022
Then he brought me some coffee and some cakes.

00:23:05.082 --> 00:23:07.703
I drank my coffee.

00:23:07.764 --> 00:23:13.058
Old man said, Mr. Sheth, I like to help people.

00:23:13.118 --> 00:23:15.188
I am a rich man.

00:23:15.249 --> 00:23:17.910
Give me your money order.

00:23:17.970 --> 00:23:21.632
I gave my money order to Mr. Sheth.

00:23:21.692 --> 00:23:26.793
Yes, this money order is worthless, he said again.

00:23:26.853 --> 00:23:30.001
But I am going to help you.

00:23:30.061 --> 00:23:33.592
I am going to change this money order for you.

00:23:33.652 --> 00:23:37.132
I am going to give you some money."

00:23:37.192 --> 00:23:40.063
Mr. Sheath went out of the room.

00:23:40.123 --> 00:23:42.644
I felt very happy again.

00:23:42.704 --> 00:23:46.705
After a few minutes, the tall man came into the room.

00:23:46.765 --> 00:23:48.946
He gave me an envelope.

00:23:49.006 --> 00:23:51.266
This is from Mr. Sheath.

00:23:51.326 --> 00:23:56.279
You can go now, the tall man said.

00:23:56.340 --> 00:24:00.153
I went out of the house.

00:24:00.213 --> 00:24:03.684
I walked along the road to the bus station.

00:24:03.744 --> 00:24:08.038
I opened the envelope and I took out my money.

00:24:08.098 --> 00:24:10.929
I counted the money.

00:24:10.989 --> 00:24:14.762
It was ten pounds.

00:24:14.822 --> 00:24:19.124
I thought about my only son's soul.

00:24:19.184 --> 00:24:25.680
My son's soul had sent me a money order for one hundred pounds.

00:24:25.740 --> 00:24:29.928
Mr. Chef had given me ten pounds.

00:24:29.988 --> 00:24:45.952
I felt old, and I felt poor again.

00:24:46.012 --> 00:25:06.005
Rich Man Poor Man was read by Sean Barrett and the recording produced by James Richardson at Studio AVP London.

